  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nRunning tests with tox (e.g. **./test_postgresql.sh**) fails at the setup stage of virtual environments.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n- checkout master\r\n- create virtual python environment: `virtualenv -p python3 env`\r\n- install dependencies: `pip install -e . --no-use-pep517`\r\n- run `./test_postgresql.sh`\r\n\r\nLate versions of pip do not play nicely with \"editable mode\", therefore the parameter `--no-use-pep517` must be provided to allow pip to run with editable mode enabled, nevertheless.\r\n\r\nAnother issue is further down the line: pip would also get invoked from tox, while the `tox.ini` shipped with tox makes use of the default install command, hence fails for the same reason.\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior ###\r\nI would expect the project's tests to run out of the box.\r\n\r\n### Version information\r\ntested on 0.99.3, also tested on **master**, FWIW\r\n\r\n**Platform**: \r\nDebian GNU/Linux buster, Kernel version 5.0.9\r\n\r\n**Maybe related:**\r\n#4848 \r\n\r\nI will gladly supply a fix for this issue, if so desired.",
